From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:44:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 13/18] Time the release from live cap detections at a fixed
 release point, record each attempt, and judge it from the detection log

With the new battery the belt runs near 50 mm/s and the planner's 2.8 s
plan always landed beyond x 0.70, where the arm's moves are bent by the
controller's singularity handling. The script now waits beside a fixed
release point, estimates the cap's arrival from its current position and
the previous pass's mean speed (max error 0.045 s over nine passes, against
0.092 s for a 1 s line fit), starts a non-blocking approach just in time and
triggers the armed gripper at arrival minus the drop delay. A blocking
move_line call had held the trigger back 0.4 s in run-10. Each attempt
records top-camera video and detections, and g4_analyze.py reports whether
the stone ended inside the cap and how far off it was.

