From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:13:34 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 14/18] Trigger the gripper 0.5 s before the cap arrives and
 open to 450 pulse, so the stone leaves the fingers at full opening speed

Run-11 video: with a 600 pulse target the stone only came free at the end of the
opening move, about 1.3 s after the trigger, and landed 43 mm behind the cap.
Opening to 450 pulse releases it about 0.5 s after the trigger. The arm now
arrives 0.2 s before the trigger and the arrival estimate is frozen once the
gripper is within 50 mm of the release point. Waiting above the release point
(--hover) hides the upstream belt from the camera (run-12), so it stays off.
Runs 13 and 14: stone in the moving cap, judged from the detection log and the
recorded frames.

