From 6abe532d8dfc9c742f19a4760019ebfdfb5c4c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:02:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 15/18] Move every stone without parking in between, and add a
 button window for one / all / return / stop

g4_simple.py: --count N (0 = until the mat is empty) goes from the release point
straight to the next stone and opens the gripper to the picking width on the way;
the next stone is looked up from beside the belt, where the arm does not hide the
mat. --stop-file ends after the stone in hand, --park-only only returns to park,
--speed-scale scales the pick and transfer moves. Each release is judged from the
cap's stone_inside flags within 6 s of the trigger. The trigger now leads the cap
by 0.6 s (runs 13-26: the stone sat 1-4 mm behind the cap centre).
g4_ui.py / g4_ui.sh: a Tk window that runs the script and shows its progress.
Robot runs: run-27 (two stones, 22.9 s per stone at 51 mm/s instead of 42.5 s),
and the window's move-all with a stop request after 38 s (two stones, parked).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
