From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:17:54 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] Skip stones the arm cannot reach, and stop a misread
 start flag from locking out the gripper loop

find_stone now takes the nearest stone whose over-stone and grasp poses pass IK
and reports the rest (the window's runs at 14:04-14:05 aborted four times on a
stone at x 0.706). ensure_loop re-reads the start flag, and when the DRL is
playing and the alive counter advances it restores the flag instead of calling
start_resident_loop, which clears the flag before it finds the DRL busy (14:12:
every run after one bad read ended in DRL_BUSY). RuntimeError codes are reported
as abort reasons. The window gets start-up options for speed, recording and a
timed stop, used to exercise every control on the robot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017S6YdmFKKoiWXK3fg85cfX
