From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:32:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] Release 5 mm further along the belt than the point the
 cap timing is aimed at

--x-offset-m (default 0.005) moves the release point to x 0.675 while the
arrival time is still computed for the cap centre reaching x 0.670, so the
stone falls 5 mm downstream of the cap centre. In the 13 successful runs the
stone settled 1.7 mm upstream of the centre on average and the cap came 0.041 s
early. The analyzer reads the aimed x from the plan. Run-28: in the cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017S6YdmFKKoiWXK3fg85cfX
