From 349dfa141806737195ede77196e31d3a82822bca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chhowm <chhowm@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:45:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Make the stop button act while waiting for the cap, and
 put a held stone back on the mat instead of parking with it

The stop file was only read after a release, so a stop pressed while the arm
waited beside the belt did nothing until the 45 s wait ran out, and the run then
parked still holding the stone (window run at 14:40, stop pressed at 14:41).
It is now read in the cap wait, before the approach and before each pick. A run
that ends without releasing puts the stone back where it was picked, then parks;
the summary says whether a stone is still held. Once the approach has started
the stone is still released. Dry runs: stop seen 0.05 s after the file appeared.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017S6YdmFKKoiWXK3fg85cfX
